{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\nThe Gerrit Verify matrix runs the same default-tier marker selection on Ubuntu Python 3.11, 3.12, and 3.13. Every cell currently enables pytest-cov and independently enforces the same repository-wide fail-under floor. All three cells remain necessary for supported-Python behavioral and contractual compatibility, but tracing identical source on three cells adds runner occupancy without a distinct verdict. Production code has no sys.version_info or sys.version branches. The closed ropeable-hydrated-siskin ticket established the accepted precedent of retaining platform tests while collecting coverage only on a primary cell.\n\n## Plan\n- Measure instrumentation cost on the same checkout and host with identical tests/unit selection and worker count: one untimed warm-up, then A-B-B-A-A-B where A includes the production coverage flags and B omits only those flags. Report local_delta = median(A elapsed) - median(B elapsed).\n- For the first post-merge Verify run, compute each changed cell delta as the matching default-suite step duration from this change own pre-merge Verify run minus the post-merge step duration. Sum only Python 3.11 and 3.12 deltas as Ubuntu runner-seconds freed; report Python 3.13 and macOS unchanged controls separately. Do not present summed parallel time as critical-path wall time, and label the single-run CI comparison as noisy.\n- Survey Django, NumPy, and SciPy current CI workflows and search tracker history. OSS consensus means at least two of these three projects selectively collect coverage on a primary or dedicated configuration while broader compatibility cells run uninstrumented, and none documents rejecting that practice for coverage or reliability.\n- Extend tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py with a workflow contract that expands the declared matrix and proves all four cells retain both default and integration pytest tiers. The contract must prove exactly Ubuntu Python 3.13 receives both coverage flags and the other three cells receive neither.\n- Encode the condition with the non-empty coverage flag string in the truthy and-slot and the empty string only in the final or-slot. This explicitly avoids the GitHub Actions empty-string-falsy trap recorded on ropeable-hydrated-siskin. Defect-seed the prior all-Ubuntu condition and a zero-coverage condition; each must make the held-out contract RED before restoring GREEN.\n- Update the coverage rationale comment in .github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml and the canonical topology in docs/coverage.md so both state that Ubuntu Python 3.13 alone collects branch coverage and enforces fail-under.\n- Run focused workflow tests, lint, and typecheck; land through Gerrit. The changed reusable workflow is resolved from main during pre-merge workflow_dispatch, so inspect resolved command lines and savings on the next Verify run after merge.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The A-B-B-A-A-B experiment reports raw elapsed samples and local_delta using the stated median formula.\n- [ ] Ubuntu Python 3.11 retains the default-tier pytest step.\n- [ ] Ubuntu Python 3.11 retains the integration-tier pytest step.\n- [ ] Ubuntu Python 3.12 retains the default-tier pytest step.\n- [ ] Ubuntu Python 3.12 retains the integration-tier pytest step.\n- [ ] Ubuntu Python 3.13 retains both pytest tiers.\n- [ ] macOS Python 3.13 retains both pytest tiers.\n- [ ] Ubuntu Python 3.13 collects branch coverage and enforces the unchanged fail-under threshold.\n- [ ] No other matrix cell receives a coverage flag.\n- [ ] The workflow contract is observed RED with the prior all-Ubuntu coverage condition.\n- [ ] The workflow contract is observed RED when no cell receives coverage.\n- [ ] At least two of the three named OSS projects match selective coverage collection.\n- [ ] No surveyed project documents rejecting selective coverage collection for reliability or coverage.\n- [ ] Tracker history cites ropeable-hydrated-siskin and any prior rejection found.\n- [ ] The workflow rationale comment describes the one-cell coverage topology.\n- [ ] docs/coverage.md describes the one-cell coverage topology.\n- [ ] Focused tests pass.\n- [ ] Lint passes.\n- [ ] Typecheck passes.\n- [ ] Gerrit LLM-Review is +1 with zero unresolved comments.\n- [ ] Gerrit Verified is +1 before merge.\n- [ ] The first post-merge Verify report applies the stated per-cell and summed runner-seconds formula and labels sample limitations.\n- [ ] Back-out is a Gerrit revert restoring coverage flags on all Ubuntu cells."}},"env_id":"0993f6a8-7a6a-4707-a671-c5bbb2691444","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786703105063981001,"uuid":"e8e87c9c-0294-4501-90a1-e24c9b9ba8a5"}